  "result": "Perfect! All 260 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the credit notes feature:\n\n**Created src/credits.js:**\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` \u2014 creates a credit note for refunds:\n  - Validates invoice status (must be 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'; NOT_ISSUED error for draft)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Validates amount doesn't exceed invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error)\n  - Generates credit note number with format: CN-<year>-<counter>\n    - Separate counter from invoices (independent numbering)\n    - Resets annually\n    - Zero-padded 4-digit counter\n  - Returns ok(creditNote) with: { number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }\n\n**Updated src/errors.js:**\n- Added `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` \u2014 for credit amounts exceeding invoice total\n- Updated `NOT_ISSUED` message to be more generic for use by both payments and credit notes\n\n**Comprehensive test coverage (260 tests total; 20 new):**\n- Valid credit note creation for all issued statuses (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Error handling (draft invoices, invalid amounts, excessive credits)\n- Amount validation (positive integers only, no zero/negative)\n- Credit note numbering:\n  - Sequential within year\n  - Annual reset\n  - Proper zero-padding\n  - Mixed with invoice numbers\n- Multiple credits for same invoice\n- Preservation of invoice data (invoice number, customer ID)\n- Reason and date handling\n- Large invoice support\n\nAll house rules followed: positive integer amounts, Result pattern for errors, no argument mutation, all tests passing.",
